WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.328 --> 00:00:03.411
(gentle piano music)

00:00:06.728 --> 00:00:08.760
- I'm the first woman to
graduate with a Doctorate

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.739
from Julliard, and now
I play the toy piano.

00:00:12.739 --> 00:00:16.000
Life works in mysterious ways.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.083
(gentle piano music)

00:00:21.198 --> 00:00:25.365
I have transformed the toy
piano into a real instrument.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:32.592
To play the toy piano well,
you have to practice on it

00:00:32.592 --> 00:00:37.331
every bit as hard as you
would on a normal piano.

00:00:37.331 --> 00:00:39.493
In fact, I think you
have to work even harder,

00:00:39.493 --> 00:00:42.192
because the action is so primitive.

00:00:42.192 --> 00:00:44.242
You can make it sound beautiful.

00:00:44.242 --> 00:00:46.992
You can make it sound convincing.

00:00:49.153 --> 00:00:53.352
It's a bit like going down the rabbit hole

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:56.852
and taking your audience with you way back

00:00:58.624 --> 00:00:59.957
down this avenue

00:01:02.732 --> 00:01:04.692
to your childhood days.

00:01:04.692 --> 00:01:08.132
(dramatic piano music)

00:01:08.132 --> 00:01:10.403
(horns honking and squeaking)

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.453
(audience laughs)

00:01:11.453 --> 00:01:15.620
Once a skeptical person
comes to a toy piano concert

00:01:16.653 --> 00:01:20.632
that I give, I'm able to turn 'em around.

00:01:20.632 --> 00:01:22.453
(applause)

00:01:22.453 --> 00:01:26.620
It's a whole extended family
now of people into toy pianos.

00:01:28.512 --> 00:01:31.011
It's a fearless little
band who are willing to

00:01:31.011 --> 00:01:33.803
stick their necks out for toys.

00:01:33.803 --> 00:01:36.886
(gentle piano music)

00:01:43.773 --> 00:01:46.773
(delicate jingling)

